  "finding": {
    "root_cause": "qf_attn.kv_head_merge divides the solved query rows by the q_norm EFFECTIVE gain (1 + weight, the factor Qwen3_5RMSNorm.forward applies).  Qwen3.5-4B layer 27's q_norm has one coordinate -- index 1 -- whose bf16 weight is exactly -1.0, so that gain is exactly 0.  Coordinate 1 is the real half of rotary plane 1, so the gain-scaled row is zero while the plane is not, and the complex coefficient qf_solve.joint_relation_solve applies to the plane returns a non-zero value into that row.  non-zero / 0 = +-Inf.",
    "chain": [
      "child q_proj carries +-Inf in one row per query head (kv-only: 16 rows x 2560 = 40960 entries; full-group: 8 x 2560 = 20480, and the energy-weighted sum of +Inf and -Inf makes those NaN)",
      "q_proj_out is non-finite for that coordinate at every token",
      "q_norm's rsqrt(mean(x^2)) over the head is then Inf, and Inf * 0 is NaN, so the whole head's query is NaN",
      "logits, softmax and the attention output are NaN, so 100% of the gated o_proj input stream is non-finite",
      "A^T A is all NaN; lam = 1e-6 * mean(diag(G)) is NaN; G + lam I is all NaN; cholesky reports 'the leading minor of order 1 is not positive-definite', which is about channel 0 only because that is where LAPACK looks first"
    ],
    "why_layer_27_and_not_3_to_23": "parent_norm_gain_census: layer 27 is the ONLY full-attention layer of this parent with an effective q_norm gain of exactly zero",
    "both_arms_affected": true,
    "fix": "qf_attn.unfold_gain installs the PARENT's own raw row at a zero-gain coordinate instead of dividing.  The score is unchanged (the norm multiplies that coordinate by zero either way) and the per-token RMS the norm divides the head by is the parent's.  Recorded per layer as zero_gain_coordinates.",
    "defence_in_depth": "qf_solve.prior_anchored_gram now refuses with the offending channels named; law_abiding_solve* fall back per rung to eigen_anchored_gram with an explicit recorded eigenvalue floor (solver_fallback); qf_attn._resolve_writer drops and counts non-finite captured rows (stream_repair)."
  }
